# Preto Loop for Cursor

When the user asks to create or design an agent loop, or asks for an iterative biomechanics, data-science, markerless-video, testing, or vailá coding workflow, read and follow `skills/preto-loop/SKILL.md`.

Use the `$preto-loop` behavior even though Cursor rules do not expose Codex's `$skill` syntax. Write the resulting loop specification to the user-selected location; do not execute it automatically.

Preserve the vailá gates: units and coordinate frames, sampling/frame rate, leakage controls, deterministic checks, GUI/CLI parity, Python metadata, pytest/Ruff/Ty validation, and explicit human approval for irreversible actions.
